1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,959
Number five we have christmas jumpers.
第五个，我们有圣诞毛衣。

2
00:00:02,959 --> 00:00:12,799
It doesn't matter where you come from what kind of background posh unpos um serious funny outgoing introverted.
不管你来自哪里、什么背景，讲究或不讲究，严肃或搞笑，外向或内向，

3
00:00:12,799 --> 00:00:21,190
Like if you work at a really strict office building or you work at the pub like I just feel like everybody embraces the christmas jumper.
无论你在规矩严格的办公楼还是酒吧工作，我就觉得大家都喜欢参与穿圣诞毛衣。

4
00:00:21,200 --> 00:00:28,320
And I love it it's wholesome it's cute some of them are really funny some of them are like actually gorgeous I just love it.
我很喜欢，温馨又可爱；有些很搞笑，有些真的很漂亮。我就是喜欢。

5
00:00:28,320 --> 00:00:37,120
Feels like no matter what kind of background or where in the country you come from or whatever so many people get involved in the christmas jumper and I love it.
无论什么背景、来自英国哪里，很多人都会加入穿圣诞毛衣这件事，我很喜欢。

6
00:00:37,120 --> 00:00:43,440
Whether you have like a day where everyone wears them at work or you have a christmas work party and people wear them out.
可能是上班时大家约好一天一起穿，也可能是在公司的圣诞聚会上穿出去，

7
00:00:43,440 --> 00:00:51,920
Or you're at the pub and everybody's wearing them or um my mom was here last week we have a little like early christmas celebration together.
或者在酒吧里，大家都穿着。嗯，我妈妈上周来了，我们一起提前过了个圣诞节。

8
00:00:51,920 --> 00:01:02,320
And we did lots of walking and every time we were out walking we were you know local or in london on the train wherever there was always somebody with a christmas jumper.
我们走了很多路，每次出去，无论本地、伦敦还是火车上，总能看到有人穿圣诞毛衣。

9
00:01:02,320 --> 00:01:08,480
I just think it's great number six a weird british christmas tradition try saying that five times fast.
我就觉得很好。第六个，一个奇特的英国圣诞传统——试着快速连说五遍。

10
00:01:08,480 --> 00:01:13,840
Pigs in blankets everything here in the uk I feel like every year there's more and more.
各种“香肠裹培根”味的东西。在英国，我感觉每年都越来越多。

11
00:01:13,840 --> 00:01:22,880
Like the obsession with this flavor profile just more and more obviously you have pigs and blankets of course absolutely wonderful fantastic.
对这种口味的着迷似乎越来越强烈。当然，真正那道香肠小吃本身非常棒。

12
00:01:22,880 --> 00:01:30,079
I want them a but when they start hauling out like all of the other christmas stuff like the sweets and the crisps.
她表示自己很喜欢；可是当商家开始搬出其他圣诞食品，比如糖果和薯片，

13
00:01:30,079 --> 00:01:41,509
And it's just like everything is pigs in blankets flavor did you know that we have pigs and blankets in north america spoiler alert yes but they look like this.
好像全是这个口味。你知道北美也有叫 pigs and blankets 的东西吗？答案是有，但长这样。

14
00:01:41,519 --> 00:01:48,880
Similar not the same so instead of the bacon they're like wrapped in a pastry to be honest they're absolutely wonderful.
相似，但不一样：北美版不是培根，而是裹着酥皮。老实说，也非常好吃。

15
00:01:48,880 --> 00:01:53,919
I haven't had them in so you know what maybe I'll make them this year I don't think I've ever actually made them.
我已经好久没吃了。你知道吗，也许今年我会做一点；我觉得自己以前其实从没做过。

16
00:01:53,919 --> 00:01:59,919
Normally like in the supermarkets you can buy packages of british pigs and blankets.
通常在超市里能买到包装好的英式香肠裹培根。

17
00:01:59,919 --> 00:02:09,519
You can in north america buy them like rolled up and stuff obviously you're not going to get them here but maybe I make them because they are they're good in their own way absolutely fab.
在北美能买到卷好的那种；这里显然不一定买得到，也许我会自己做，因为它们自有好吃的地方，很棒。

18
00:02:09,519 --> 00:02:16,079
But in north america you're not going to get pigs and blankets flavored crisps that is uniquely british.
但按她的经验，北美没有这个口味的薯片，她觉得这很有英国特色。

19
00:02:16,079 --> 00:02:28,799
While we are talking about food number seven is simply food choices now christmas dinner in canada in america in the uk there's definitely some overlap but they are not the same.
既然说到吃的，第七个就是食物选择。加拿大、美国和英国的圣诞晚餐确实有重合，但并不完全一样。

20
00:02:28,799 --> 00:02:36,160
There's a lot of interesting food choices around christmas here in the uk not just like christmas dinner but just like christmas in general.
她觉得英国圣诞期间有很多有趣的食物选择；不只是晚餐，而是整个圣诞季的饮食。

21
00:02:36,160 --> 00:02:45,120
Some of them I absolutely love some I will hate until the day that I die but whether I love them or hate them some of the ones that stand out to me.
有些我非常喜欢，有些我会讨厌一辈子。不过无论喜不喜欢，以下这些让我印象深刻。

22
00:02:45,120 --> 00:02:53,040
Are parsnips Yorkshire pudding brussels sprouts in any variety bread sauce.
比如欧洲防风草根、约克郡布丁、各种做法的抱子甘蓝，还有面包酱。

23
00:02:53,040 --> 00:03:03,279
Christmas pudding not to be confused with christmas cake minced pies custard Brandy butter not to be confused with Brandy cream.
圣诞布丁，别和圣诞蛋糕搞混；还有圣诞甜馅饼、卡仕达酱和白兰地黄油，别和白兰地奶油搞混。

24
00:03:03,279 --> 00:03:12,719
A very small selection of ones I feel are uniquely british whether you love them or hate them they're they're special except parsnips.
这只是她觉得很英式的一小部分。无论喜欢还是讨厌，它们都很特别——除了欧洲防风草根。

25
00:03:12,719 --> 00:03:21,589
I hate parsnips I don't understand people who like parsnips okay it's come that time of the video where I'm starting to lose feeling in my legs.
我讨厌欧洲防风草根，不懂为什么有人喜欢。好吧，视频又录到我开始腿麻的时候了。

26
00:03:21,599 --> 00:03:31,279
What number are we on eight a british thing that is quite interesting that I'd never experienced back in canada and that is sending cards to everyone.
讲到第几个了？第八个，一件她在加拿大没经历过、觉得很有趣的英国习惯：给大家寄贺卡。

27
00:03:31,279 --> 00:03:38,640
I don't think I had ever sent a christmas card in canada like not not one.
我觉得自己在加拿大从没寄过圣诞卡，一张都没有。

28
00:03:38,640 --> 00:03:47,510
And the thought process is like well what's the point of sending my grandma a christmas card when I'm going to see her at christmas and give her presents.
我的想法是，既然圣诞节要见奶奶、给她礼物，给她寄圣诞卡还有什么意义呢？

29
00:03:47,520 --> 00:03:49,680
Like why am I sending her a card it makes no sense.
我为什么还要寄卡给她？我觉得说不通。

30
00:03:49,680 --> 00:03:56,880
But here I find in the uk whether you are seeing that person at christmas or not you are still sending a christmas card.
但我发现在英国，无论圣诞节见不见这个人，仍然会寄一张圣诞卡。

31
00:03:56,880 --> 00:04:07,440
And if you want to be quintessentially british you're going to write really personal like family information like about your parents or your kids or yourself.
她还打趣说，如果想特别英式，就在卡上写些很私人的家庭近况，比如父母、孩子或自己的事情。

32
00:04:07,440 --> 00:04:14,240
In these cards it combines the british love of christmas and gossip into one activity.
在这些卡片里写近况，在她看来，就是把对圣诞节和闲聊八卦的喜爱结合成了一项活动。
